            <ArticleTitle>Are Gut Microbes Responsible for Post-dieting Weight Rebound?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1550-4131(16)30649-0</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cmet.2016.12.016</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>One of the dieting conundrums in the age of the obesity epidemic is the cycle of weight loss and regain known as the &quot;yo-yo effect.&quot; Thaiss et al. (2016) demonstrate that the microbiome plays a key role in this phenomenon and that simple dietary supplementations can reset the weight-rebound clock.</AbstractText>
